 "final_text": "Submitted. Summary for Robin's brief:\n\n**Caterpillar leverage section**\n- **LT debt (FY2024):** $27.35B\n- **Equity (FY2024):** $19.49B\n- **3-year LT D/E ratio picture:** FY2022 1.62 \u2192 FY2023 1.25 \u2192 FY2024 1.40 (avg **1.43**) \u2014 leverage spiked in 2022, eased in 2023 on an equity rebuild, then ticked back up in 2024 as debt grew faster than equity.\n- **Internal relationship:** We don't currently trade with Caterpillar \u2014 no AR/AP record in Books or the ERP customer/vendor master, and no contracts or correspondence on file. Any deal would start as new-customer onboarding, not an extension of existing terms.\n\nBoth the filings figures and the \"no relationship\" finding were independently cross-checked (different data-pull methods / fuzzy name searches) and held up with no discrepancies. One data-quality note worth flagging to Robin: the environment's SEC filings snapshot only carries the \"including noncontrolling interest\" equity tag rather than pure `StockholdersEquity`, so the equity figures above are very slightly inclusive of NCI \u2014 immaterial for Caterpillar historically, but worth a footnote if precision matters for the deck.",
